  "releaseNotes": "0.1.0-preview.6: First public preview. Ships FipsDeploymentMarker so hosts can declare a FIPS 140-3 operating posture, plus runtime checks that fail fast when the active cryptographic provider does not match the declared posture. The actual FIPS-validated ML-KEM implementation must be supplied by the consumer (e.g. BouncyCastle FIPS, a vendor-validated module, or — on a future SDK — the .NET FIPS-validated provider).",
